    },
    {
      "id": "488b7k5",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>EXAM CRITICAL — BSA 2023 (Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam replaces Indian Evidence Act 1872):</strong></p><p>• Section 2(1)(d) defines Electronic Record including SMS, email, social media posts as evidence</p><p>• Section 63 — electronic evidence admissible with certificate from responsible official</p><p>• Section 23 — confessions to police not admissible (same as earlier Sec 25 IEA)</p><p>• Section 24 — confession under threat/promise not admissible</p><p>• Section 57 — court may take judicial notice of central &amp; state laws</p><p>• Digital/electronic records now treated on par with physical documents</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
